From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:20:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Draw the 3D view for each eye with a stereo preference

With "stereo 3D view" in the 3D view preferences, the default surface
format asks for stereo buffers, and the view is drawn once into the left
buffer and once into the right buffer from the same scene data. The eye
separation is a percentage of the distance to the point looked at and
changes at once. Picking uses the camera between the eyes. Centering on
a double click reads the depth of the eye that was drawn last, so it
unprojects with that eye's camera. Without stereo buffers the view stays
the single normal view.

All of it is in the new class Stereo3dView. It asks for the stereo
buffers in configureOpenGLContext(), where the preference is read from
the settings file because the format must be known before the window is
created. Around GLView::paintGL() it sets GLView::stereoEyeOffset from
currentTargetBuffer(), which needs Qt 6.5, and the eye separation is
read from the settings only there; the preferences ask for a redraw when
it changes. With older Qt the class is a stub that never asks for
stereo buffers and never moves the eye, so the offset stays 0. The Qt
version is checked only in Stereo3dView.h and Stereo3dView.cc.

